plication/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"942e86e0790e7daba76689e96c10dccd2ef58561927d22b1436d5e24986aa309","event_uuid":"bc30644d-7f0c-4a95-a41c-0b1c834d5655","position":{"commit_sha":"40e46284885940a45ccb2b86fc8a9234971724f8","position":"1785778352891609001-bc30644d-7f0c-4a95-a41c-0b1c834d5655"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"dc35369a-6e34-424d-af99-7efeb92004fa","comments":[],"created_at":1785560978283491001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"312a6680-49d9-4c14-b0ac-b1c8effe88b6","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"343b-4fdc-6722-469b"},{"link_uuid":"dd35f09a-c849-471b-ba23-461a7c8a9ab3","relation":"blocks","target_id":"061c-ecd1-8967-4a76"}],"description":"# Code-review verdicts never record provider_provenance\n\n## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/llm/code_review/sidecar.py:106` reads `verdict.get(\"provider_provenance\")`, but the\ncode-review verdict NEVER sets that key, so every signed code-review verdict records it as absent.\nThis is the SAME defect that story 343b found and fixed for the plan-review and completion gates\n(343b gap 5); code review was left out of that change deliberately to keep it reviewable.\n\nVERIFIED IN SOURCE at commit b872bc3c89:\n- The terminal verdict is assembled by `code_review_coach`\n  (`src/rebar/llm/code_review/workflow_ops.py:500-532`); its return dict carries\n  verdict/blocking/advisory/coaching/coverage/dropped/indeterminate and no provenance.\n- `finalize_code_review_verdict` then adds only cfg-derived fields:\n  `verdict.setdefault(\"runner\", runner_sel.name)` and `verdict.setdefault(\"model\", cfg.model)`\n  (`src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py:244-245`). Exactly the cfg-derived shape 343b removed\n  from plan-review.\n- The outage path `_degraded_code_review_verdict` (`workflow/gate_dispatch.py:246-257`) sets\n  `runner` only.\n\nCONSEQUENCE: the epic's acceptance criterion \"A signed verdict states which provider, endpoint host,\nand support tier produced it\" holds for two of the three gates. A code-review verdict produced\nthrough Bedrock, or behind an OpenAI-compatible gateway, still records only a bare model string --\nthe misattribution the provenance record exists to remove. This matters most for the review bot,\nwhich is the S8 Bedrock cutover target.\n\n## Approach\nMirror what 343b did, and reuse its mechanism rather than inventing a second one:\n`capabilities.provenance_for` assembles the record ONCE inside the runner\n(`src/rebar/llm/runner.py:388`) and `findings.finalize_outcome` stamps it onto every per-call\nresult (`findings.py:312-313,343-344`). An AGENT step's outputs are the runner result VERBATIM\n(`workflow/runs.py:262`), and 343b made `_dispatch` default the key to None when no provider\nresolved, so `${{ steps.<agent>.outputs.provider_provenance }}` resolves for code review too.\n\nSo the shape is: wire the record from code review's own Pass-2 `verify` agent step through to\nwhatever assembles the terminal verdict, and set the key only when it is present.\n\nDO NOT recompute the record at the verdict site. `capabilities.provenance_for`'s docstring\n(`capabilities.py:295-300`) forbids it: a recomputed record can diverge from the one that actually\ndrove the run, which is the prior regression it must not repeat.\n\nDO NOT try to carry it through the usage aggregate. `sizing.usage_record` (`sizing.py:272-290`)\nbuilds each per-call record from the runner result's `_usage` SUB-DICT only, and the provenance\nlives at the result's TOP level, so it is dropped before aggregation. 343b established this dead\nend; do not re-derive it.\n\nHONEST VALUE WHERE NOTHING RAN: `_degraded_code_review_verdict` is the outage path -- no model ran,\nso it must OMIT the key rather than synthesize one from cfg. 343b applies the same rule at its three\nno-record sites.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py` (298 LOC) and/or\n  `src/rebar/llm/code_review/workflow_ops.py` -- whichever holds the assembly seam.\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/code-review.yaml` -- the wire from the verify step.\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py:246-257` -- the outage path, comment only.\n- a test file under `tests/unit/`.\n\n## Testing\nTHE ORACLE MUST NOT HAND-BUILD A VERDICT. That is precisely why 343b gap 5 shipped broken: every\ntest handed `build_payload` a verdict that already contained the key, proving the persist step and\nnever the path. Model the tests on `tests/unit/test_verdict_provenance_wiring.py`:\n- assert the gate YAML actually WIRES the record, from a step that is an AGENT step (only an agent\n  step's outputs are the runner result verbatim; sourcing from a scripted op silently wires None);\n- assert on a verdict produced by the REAL assembly path, then fed to the REAL sidecar payload\n  builder;\n- a control asserting the outage path omits the key rather than inventing one.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] a test asserts a code-review verdict produced by the real assembly path carries\n      `provider_provenance`, and that the real sidecar payload built FROM that verdict records it\n- [ ] a test asserts `code-review.yaml` wires the record from an AGENT step, not a scripted op\n- [ ] a test asserts the degraded/outage code-review verdict OMITS the key rather than deriving one\n      from cfg\n- [ ] `grep -n \"setdefault(\\\"model\\\"\" src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py` is accompanied by a\n      provenance assignment, i.e. the verdict no longer records a bare model string alone\n- [ ] every file touched stays at or under the 800-LOC cap in `.github/module-size-limit.txt`","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["blocks","061c-ecd1-8967-4a76"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6a00bd62-9976-44bb-ae90-4974d49d496f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"e951-7df6-1851-4d5e","ticket_type":"task","title":"Code-review verdicts never record provider_provenance","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["10e37bbd-5a6e-4f4c-8663-d0a524f62e2c","312a6680-49d9-4c14-b0ac-b1c8effe88b6","dd35f09a-c849-471b-ba23-461a7c8a9ab3","8ad09369-8334-4959-93d7-f83b2d6c97d1","6a00bd62-9976-44bb-ae90-4974d49d496f","bc30644d-7f0c-4a95-a41c-0b1c834d5655"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785778352891609002,"uuid":"752688a6-57a0-4bf0-abc0-33c7b5d1bdf4"}